    "significance": "Intracortical BCIs have decoded speech and movement in lab settings, but clinical viability requires unsupervised, at-home operation with stable performance over months. This paper demonstrates that an implanted electrode array can be used independently by a patient outside the clinic, decoding both speech intent and cursor movement reliably without daily recalibration or technician support. This is a critical proof point that neurotechnology devices can transition from research demonstrations to practical tools that paralyzed users can operate autonomously in their own homes, directly advancing the path to FDA approval and patient adoption.",
